        "id": 31076,
        "name": "lugaru",
        "username": "lugaru",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lugaru/{size}/2767_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-22T16:41:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Ronway&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Ronway\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wait just one minute there people, there are hobbies outside of gaming? I don’t believe any of it for a minute.</p>\n<p>In all honesty though I don’t really have any other hobby. Video Games are a fairly expensive budget and between rent, food, and a one and a half year old I don’t even have much money to spend on that.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’ve gotten really into indy games… they tend to be cheap and provide a lot of value. Minecraft is the obvious example, but right now I’m big on Project Zomboid. It is a cheap game, still in alfa but very playable, and you cant win. It actually says “this is the story of how you died” at the start. Each game is fairly unique… sometimes you will slowly go mad in an attic, running out of food, sometimes you will go down in a blaze of glory, killing dozens of zombies in a burning building.</p>",
