      {
        "id": 31077,
        "name": "WriterRyan",
        "username": "WriterRyan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/writerryan/{size}/2710_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-22T18:37:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Tamar&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Tamar\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Coding is too much like learning a foreign language, which I’m terrible at, but I’m glad other people do it so I have things like games and the internets!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’d go a step further and say that coding is like learning a foreign language, except if you screw up your grammar in a foreign language the person you’re talking to doesn’t just yell “WRONG” over and over again until you give up and walk away. (I dropped out of a CS major and then a CS minor when I realized I hated it.)</p>\n<p>I enjoy playing video games when I have the time, and I’ve discovered that I actually like doing home improvement projects. I also like reading, going to live concerts, and writing whenever the fancy takes me.</p>\n<p>By the way, lugaru, I like your site’s logo a lot.</p>",
