      {
        "id": 31091,
        "name": "Nilus",
        "username": "Nilus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nilus/{size}/2099_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-23T21:02:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I use to be a video game/PC gamer but when I got to the point in career where I spend 50 to 60 hours a week looking at a computer screen I decided to give them up mostly.  Also use to role play a lot when I was younger but not so much in the last few years.</p>\n<p>My two current hobbies/jobs are</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Being a Dad to a awesome 4 year old son.  He is not quite old enough for SOTM yet but this summer we plan to start expanding his Board game collection to include some more interesting game(Thinking of trying “That’s my Fish”)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>I am a Malifaux Henchman and playtester.   Malifaux is a skirmish level steampunk, horror, minature game with some really cool unique rules.   And a Henchman is what they call there demo team guys(Like a Press Ganger for Privateer Press, or an Outrider for Games workshop).  I have been doing that since the game was released in 2009.   Along with demoing the game I also run events.  I am the lead person in charge of all the Malifaux events at Adepticon and I have recently been asked and accepted the job to run all the Malifaux tournament events at Gencon this year.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>",
